**Additional Job Description**
**Core responsibilities as a Manager (PiD Specialist) would entail (but not be limited to)**
As a Manager (PiD Specialist) in the team, you’ll be at the heart of our delivery on some of the most complex and high-profile transactions in the market. You will work closely with colleagues to support with leading client engagements, managing workstreams, and acting as a trusted advisor to client stakeholders.


Drawing on your people expertise, you’ll help organisations navigate critical workforce challenges across the deal lifecycle — from planning and execution to integration and transformation.


You will also play a pivotal role in developing our people, shaping propositions, and driving business development opportunities, ensuring that our practice continues to grow and succeed.


**Your Responsibilities May Include**

* Direct interaction with and ability to build trusted relationships with People leaders and other senior business stakeholders;
* Managing workstream delivery to time, quality, and budget, while providing insight and lessons learned from previous projects;
* Coaching and developing colleagues at all levels, providing feedback and guidance to enhance technical, interpersonal, and consulting skills across the team;
* Working with cross-functional PwC teams to bring integrated solutions to client challenges;
* Driving business development by scoping people related activities on transactions, contributing to proposals, and shaping compelling client propositions;
* Supporting the development of our practice through thought leadership, knowledge sharing, and sector-specific initiatives.

**What You Will Gain**
You will have the opportunity to work alongside a high-performing, UK-based People in Deals team. This collaborative environment will enable you to learn from experienced professionals, share best practices, and contribute directly to global deal-related activities;


By engaging with colleagues across borders, you will gain valuable international exposure, enhance your understanding of global deals and broaden your professional perspective;


The opportunity to take an important role on challenging and complex projects, working directly with client stakeholders;


The chance to deepen your expertise in both the strategic and technical aspects of workforce related issues within a transaction, while also developing your leadership and business development skills;


Exposure to multiple sectors, client types, and deal contexts, giving you a broad and varied career path within PwC;


A supportive and collaborative team environment where you’ll be empowered to take ownership and make an impact;


Ongoing training and development, including opportunities to deepen your consulting skills and specialise in areas of interest.


**Must-have Skills**
Strong stakeholder management skills, with the ability to engage credibly with the UK PiD team and client stakeholders, managing upwards effectively;


Excellent quantitative and written skills, able to build analyses or an evidence base to support a position, often in situations with imperfect or incomplete information.


Strong analytical skills and data literacy; proficiency in Excel, Power BI, or other data tools is preferred;


Ability to leverage AI and digital tools to enhance analysis, improve efficiency, and deliver innovative solutions to clients.


Ability to manage shifting timelines and ambiguous project environments;


A healthy
**curiosity**
, coupled with a disciplined approach to understanding and
**solving problems**
.


**Comfortable under pressure and managing through ambiguity**
to deliver tasks in an environment where there are many unknowns.


**Adaptable**
, and up for the challenge of mastering new sectors and developing experience across a wide range of subject areas.


**Experience**
Proven success in leading workstream delivery, managing priorities, and producing high-quality outputs ideally under the pressures of a deal environment;


Some experience of working on deals (integration, carve-out, or post-deal), ideally combined with broader business transformation experience and a people focused background;


Experience in coaching, mentoring, and performance managing teams to support with the continuous improvement of capability and performance;


Experience in consulting or professional services would be advantageous, but not essential.


**Eligibility Criteria**

* Past Experience: 5+ years of prior relevant work experience.
* Some experience in M&A or management consulting domain would be advantageous.

Rodeo FX is an award-winning creative company offering services in visual effects, animation, advertising and experiential. We partner with some of the world's leading storytellers and entertainment companies, including Netflix, HBO, Disney, Marvel, Amazon Studios, Warner Bros. and Sony.


In 2026, Rodeo FX opened its newest studio in
**Bengaluru**
, expanding our global network across Canada, the United States, Europe and India. Located in
**International Tech Park Bengaluru**
, the new 40,000-square-foot studio is designed to accommodate up to 400 artists and supports both Rodeo FX and Mikros Animation.


Our Bengaluru team is fully integrated into Rodeo FX's global pipeline, collaborating with artists, supervisors and production teams across our international studios on incredible projects.


We're now building the senior creative and technical leadership for this studio. Joining us at this stage means having the opportunity not only to contribute to world-class projects, but also to help shape the team, workflows and culture of a growing global hub.


**Job Description**
The VFX Producer ensures proper management of the budget and production schedule for every show for which they are responsible. Working with various departments, the VFX Producer ensures ongoing adherence to the schedule and budget established between production and the client.


This includes working with the VFX Supervisor and other Supervisors to establish and communicate plans and milestones for each project, communicating with clients on changes and closely following project budgets.


**Main Responsibilities**

* In collaboration with the VFX Supervisor and Business Development, participate in the evaluation of costs and bidding for potential projects;
* In conjunction with the VFX Supervisor, create a strategy and establish a global vision that will be applied throughout the VFX project, ensuring client satisfaction, cost efficiency and profit generation;
* Communicate regularly with clients on the status of projects, creating a positive and collaborative working relationship;
* Recommend and provide solutions and bids for new shots or client changes throughout the project all while ensuring respect of deadlines and budgets;
* Oversee scheduling and preparation of project plans, including performance targets and milestones. Initiate, approve and budget overtime, as needed;
* In consultation with departments, assign key talent to projects, ensuring the right mix of skills and experience to meet the project requirements. Confirm any additional necessary resources needed throughout the completion of projects;
* Responsible for supervising the progress and efficiency of projects, keeping a thorough tracking of the schedule and budget, ensuring Shotgun is up to date at all times. Ensure it is in line with the initial quote, the project plan and that it meets client requirements;
* Prepare any budget reports that may be required. Forecast scheduling and budgeting issues along with client changes that may arise.
* Maintain regular communication with the Production team on all necessary information relating to the project;
* Ensure in-person turn-overs with artists and the VFX team are completed by the Supervisors;
* Perform mid and post-mortem meetings and assessments, identify areas for improvement and ensure that all issues are addressed;
* Provide leadership to drive continuous improvement, make recommendations of best practices, suggest ways to improve, design processes to increase efficiency and ensure implementation.
* Mentor members of their team by providing training and sharing knowledge. Communicate any specific training needs to the Head of Department. May participate in preparing training materials or giving group training sessions;
* Review the performance of their production team and ensure that they receive feedback on a regular basis through the mid and post mortem process. Conduct annual performance reviews and make recommendations for salary reviews;
* In conjunction with Department Managers, responsible for the management of performance of their production team including deciding on promotions (levels and/or positions), disciplinary or performance issues, and terminations.
* Actively monitor the work climate in his/her team, taking steps to encourage and ensure the maintenance of a positive work environment and adherence to company values;
* Ensure VFX Breakdowns are created for every project;
* Positively represent Rodeo FX within the VFX and related communities, both locally and in the worldwide market, to further grow the company’s reputation as an industry leader.

**Qualifications**

* Minimum 5 years of experience in a VFX Producer role in a VFX or 3D animation studio environment, preferably on high-end feature film and/or episodic productions.
* Minimum of 15 years of production experience in visual effects;
* Excellent knowledge of GSuite and Microsoft Office;
* Strong knowledge of Shotgun project management software;
* Excellent knowledge of the VFX Production process from concept to delivery;
* Excellent organizational and planning skills;
* Excellent sense of prioritization and respect of deadlines and budgets;
* Must be available for occasional international travel.

**Additional Information**
**Diversity, Equity and Inclusion**
At Rodeo FX, diversity is a core value. We’re committed to creating an inclusive, equitable workplace where different perspectives are embraced. Every team member brings unique insight that strengthens our creativity, challenges our thinking, and helps us deliver better work.


**Use of Artificial Intelligence in Recruitment**
Rodeo FX may use AI-based tools to support certain steps of the recruitment process, such as interview transcription or preliminary application analysis. These tools may be operated by third-party providers, and data may be processed outside Quebec. These tools never replace human decision-making: all final hiring decisions are made by our recruitment team and hiring managers. To learn more about how we protect your personal information and your rights, please consult our Privacy Policy.


**Apply with LinkedIn**
If you would like to use the “Apply with LinkedIn” feature to simplify your application, please make sure you accept cookies on the SmartRecruiters application page. This allows the feature to display and function properly.

**About the Research Programme** 




 India’s urban transition is unprecedented in scale and complexity. Within it lie both the opportunities of increased economic development and employment as well as the challenges of persistent inequality, extreme deprivation and environmental degradation. The Research Programme at IIHS aims to build new knowledge that enables solutions to these challenges; transforming the everyday lives of people and the economy, society and the environment.










 The IIHS Research Office supports the Research Programme and plays a pivotal role in building research capabilities and impact. It anchors key functions such as grant seeking, grantmaking, grant management, research communications, and research ethics. The office also contributes to knowledge production and capacity development, organises conferences and workshops, and coordinates with other teams within IIHS. By managing key processes and activities, the Research Office enables collaboration between Schools and other functions.










**About the Postdoctoral Programme at IIHS** 




 The IIHS Postdoctoral Programme builds on over a decade of teaching and training young scholars and early career researchers working on urbanisation\-related questions across India’s cities, towns and villages, and across the world. These have included spaces for learning from peers as well as leading global researchers and academics, like the IIHS Doctoral Workshop and Urban ARC.










 IIHS’ Postdoctoral Programme, little over a decade old, offered candidates the opportunity to transition to IIHS positions or transition to careers at leading domestic and global universities and research institutions. It is now being refocused to create a cohort of the next generation of IIHS Faculty and contribute to interdisciplinary faculty development of other Indian higher education institutions.










**Job Description** 




 IIHS is seeking a capable and dynamic interdisciplinary professional to help redesign, drive and manage its Postdoctoral Programme. They will also assist with building emerging and established research areas at IIHS, focusing on environment and sustainability, economic development, urban and digital systems, infrastructure and services.










**Activities and Tasks** 




 Responsibilities would include, but not be limited to, the following:



* IIHS Postdoctoral Programme support:
* Support and coordination:
* The position requires strong support and coordination abilities to deliver the postdoctoral programme in conjunction with IIHS’ interdisciplinary Schools, Labs and Centres. This will include providing support for outreach, recruitment and the hiring process, supporting Postdoctoral Fellows in the Schools, Labs and Centres; and coordinating with the IIHS People Function (HR), Academic Offices and the Finance, Legal, Operations, and Communications and Design teams;
* Professional development support:
* Helping with designing and providing professional development support to Postdoctoral Fellows, as needed;
* Research support:
* Proposal development and grant writing:
* Support for emerging and established areas of research at IIHS with a focus on economic development, urban systems and infrastructure, environment and sustainability and/ or STEM disciplines;
* Establishing systems and processes:
* The role requires the candidate to help establish multiple systems and processes in conjunction with the Senior Lead – Research Office, and Deans/ Associate Deans of the IIHS Schools, and Heads of Centres and Labs. Towards this, the candidate will help build out systems, policies, and processes within the IIHS Research Office;
* General administration and programme execution:
* The candidate will help establish and administer internal faculty and postdoctoral capacity building systems. These may include, for example, designing teaching and learning materials for structured learning sessions around pedagogy, research and applied research;
* Documentation and outreach:
* The position requires strong documentation abilities. This includes documentation for statutory and non\-statutory requirements and maintaining records for regulatory purposes. The position also requires close coordination with the Research Office communications team to curate and plan internal and external communication needs;
* Other institutional responsibilities:
* Event management:
* In addition to the primary responsibilities listed above, the position is also expected to support Conferences, Workshops and other public\-facing events organised by the Research Programme;
* Institutional support:
* Providing support to other IIHS activities including academics, research, training, practice, operations and others;
* Participating in all activities of Institution\-Building at IIHS; carrying out tasks as assigned by IIHS; and traveling on IIHS work within or outside the country as and when needed.









**Structure and Reporting** 




 The incumbent will report to the Senior Lead — Research Programme at IIHS and will be required to collaborate effectively with a diverse group of internal teams and external individuals/ organisations, and students.










**Person Specification** 




 The ideal candidate should have:



* A PhD in Technical, scientific and managerial fields, with an interest in interdisciplinary and urban related work, is desired;
* Candidates with PhDs from Development Studies, Policy Studies, Social Sciences, Management, Higher Education, Urban Studies or related fields; with an interest in technical, environmental and/or scientific knowledge systems are also strongly encouraged to apply;
* A minimum of 12 years of work experience in a research or academic institution (preferably a higher education institution), with substantial time spent in faculty development and/ or capacity building programmes;
* Strong understanding of the research and academic fields especially in the Indian context;
* Strong understanding of programme management and operations;
* Good understanding of budgeting and financial management;
* The ability to collate and work with data;
* Excellent interpersonal communication and stakeholder management skills;
* Content curation skills are desirable.









 This offer is on an exclusive basis, which implies that other professional assignments (whether compensated or not) that bear a potential conflict of interest with IIHS cannot be undertaken.










 The search will remain open until the position is filled.










**Location** 




 This position is based in Bengaluru and may entail travel to other locations in India.










**Review and Assessment** 




 The role and performance of the incumbent shall be subject to normal review and assessment systems at IIHS.










**Diversity Policy** 




 IIHS is an equal opportunity employer that encourages women, people with disabilities and those from economically and socially excluded communities with the requisite skills and qualifications to apply for positions.










**Contact** 




 Please write to us at careers@iihs.co.in if you need any clarifications while filling the online application form.

**About the ASSURE (Accelerating Sustainable and Super\-Efficient Real Estate) project** 




 ASSURE is a joint initiative of the Indian Institute for Human Settlements, India’s premier knowledge institution working on urban transformation, and global next\-generational digital services and consulting major and sustainability leader Infosys. ASSURE aims to transform India’s large, rapidly growing, and carbon and energy intensive real estate sector by promoting High Performance Buildings (HPBs) at scale.










 In pursuit of its goal, ASSURE will, in the coming years, offer technical assistance to India’s largest developers for lighthouse projects spanning 100 million sq. ft., skill/ upskill 12,000 individuals, support 30 curated innovators, deliver a performance measurement and verification platform that incentivises HPB adoption and financing, and engage with policymakers and financial decisionmakers to usher enabling policies and financing arrangements for HPBs. In lighthouse projects, ASSURE works closely with developer teams to set realistic performance goals, guide technology and design choices, assist with implementation and O\&M, and navigate financial and procurement pathways — ensuring successful delivery and operation of HPBs.









**Job Description** 




 We are seeking a dynamic professional who can own and operate a Real Estate Innovation Accelerator, driving the end\-to\-end lifecycle from strategy and blueprint to market delivery and impact measurement. The mandate is to design, run, and scale 30 high\-potential real estate innovations — pilots, pilots\-to\-enterprise programs, and market\-ready offerings. The candidate will recruit and manage cohorts, coordinate cross\-functional teams, secure sponsor buy\-in, grant administration, and deliver measurable value for innovators initially and eventually for the industry clients. A background with innovation cohorts or scaling real estate pilots will be beneficial.










 This is a contractual engagement for an initial term of 11 months, renewable on mutual consent.










**Activities and Tasks** 



* Real estate innovation strategy and accelerator blueprint:
* Define and implement the Innovation Accelerator’s vision, objectives, and success criteria aligned with ASSURE goals and ecosystem needs;
* Architecting the accelerator blueprint: program cadence, cohort themes, selection criteria, mentorship/ experts network, funding models, and post\-accelerator pathways;
* Market shaping, go\-to\-market for real estate innovation:
* Analysing market demand, regulatory considerations, and stakeholder ecosystems (developers, owners, operators, lenders, regulators, tenants);
* Designing and executing the GTM for accelerator outcomes: positioning, messaging, partnerships, pilot\-to\-scale roadmaps, and enterprise adoption;
* Building compelling business cases and analyses to secure client engagement;
* Pilot design, execution and scale\-up:
* Leading end\-to\-end pilot lifecycle within the accelerator: scoping, experiment designing, governance, capturing data, learning loops, and transitioning to enterprise programs;
* Curating a portfolio of real estate pilots;
* Managing pilot intake, onboarding, measurements and scale off;
* Governance, reporting and analytics:
* Establishing governance for accelerator programs, including milestones and gate reviews;
* Developing dashboards and executive summaries to monitor pilot progress, value realisation, and risk;
* Producing data\-driven insights to optimise the accelerator portfolio and the informing of strategic pivots.
* Stakeholder engagement and communications:
* Building and nurturing relationships with developers, owners, investors, regulators, technology vendors, and internal stakeholders;
* Creating compelling proposals, progress reports, and executive presentations for boards, sponsors, and client executives;
* Representing the accelerator in industry events, thought leadership, and market forums;
* Network building and partnerships:
* Developing an ecosystem of partners (architecture/ design firms, IPCs, tech vendors, investors, academic partners, regulatory bodies) to source ideas and co\-innovate;
* Managing partnership agreements, joint pilots, and co\-innovation programs with clear value for all parties;
* Fostering communities of practice to accelerate knowledge sharing and accelerator outcomes;
* People and leadership (indirect):
* Mentoring and growing a cross\-functional team supporting the accelerator:
* Hiring selectively and building the required capabilities to scale the accelerator program;
* Institutional:
* Providing support to other IIHS activities including academics, research, training, practice, operations and others;
* Participating in all activities of institution\-building at IIHS; carrying out tasks as assigned by IIHS; and travelling on IIHS work within or outside the country as and when needed.








**Structure and Reporting** 




 The specialist will report to the Chief – Practice at IIHS or to any other person designated by the Chief – Practice and will be required to collaborate effectively with a diverse group of internal teams and external individuals/ organisations, and students.









**Person Specification** 




 The ideal candidate should have:



* A Masters degree in Engineering, Construction Management, Architecture, Business Management;
* 7\+ years of relevant experience in Innovation Scaling / Incubation / Business Development in Real Estate, or related fields;
* Experience leading accelerator programs, pilots, or platform initiatives is desirable, with a proven ability to design and operate an innovation accelerator or similar program, including selecting cohorts, mentoring, and scaling pilots to enterprise deployment;
* Strong business acumen with ability to build ROI models, pricing concepts, and business cases for innovative real estate offerings;
* Demonstrated ability to lead cross\-functional teams and manage complex stakeholder ecosystems;
* Excellent communication and presentation skills; comfortable engaging with C\-suite and multi\-stakeholder audiences;
* Familiarity with regulatory/compliance considerations in real estate and those related to the innovation scale\-up;









 This is a contractual engagement for an initial term of 11 months, renewable on mutual consent. This offer is on an exclusive basis, which implies that other professional assignments (whether compensated or not) that bear a potential conflict of interest with IIHS cannot be undertaken.










 The search will remain open until the position is filled.










